# ── Expo / React Native (apps/insolvia_app) ─────────────────────
# Expo's local cache: the dev server's resolved config, Metro's transform
# cache, and the generated web `.expo/types`. Regenerated on every `expo
# start`, never committed.
.expo/
# `expo export` output. Anchored per app for the same reason the Node build
# output below is: a bare `dist/` would silently swallow any future build
# directory anywhere in the repo.
/apps/insolvia_app/dist/

# GENERATED, NOT ABSENT. `ios/` and `android/` are the native projects `expo
# prebuild` writes from app.json — the Continuous Native Generation workflow
# (https://docs.expo.dev/workflow/continuous-native-generation/). They are
# build output derived from committed config, so committing them would mean
# hand-maintaining two copies of every native setting and resolving prebuild's
# diffs by hand forever.
#
# There is nothing to ignore today: the app is a web SPA and no prebuild has
# run (see the Xcode/CocoaPods note in scripts/dev-setup.sh). These lines are
# here so that the day mobile starts, a `git add -A` cannot sweep 40 MB of
# generated Xcode/Gradle project into a commit before anyone notices.
/apps/insolvia_app/ios/
/apps/insolvia_app/android/

*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/
coverage/
*.log

# ── Terraform ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfvars                # real vars are secret; *.tfvars.example IS committed
infra/envs/ci-trust/terraform.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
# .terraform.lock.hcl IS committed — one per root under infra/envs/, so every
# checkout and CI run installs the same provider build (infra/CLAUDE.md owns
# the upgrade procedure). Module-level locks are different: running init in a
# module dir (the pre-commit validate hook does) writes one, but only the env
# roots' locks are the record — the module copies are noise.
infra/modules/*/.terraform.lock.hcl
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
# Lambda zips built by archive_file at plan time.
infra/modules/*/.build/

# Per-machine local wiring written by scripts/dev-aws-setup.sh (the shared dev
# pool's ids, the Google client id — no secrets, but machine-specific and never
# committed). There is deliberately no `.example` alongside these: every value
# names a resource that exists outside this repo, so a copied template would
# name nothing. Run `./scripts/dev-aws-setup.sh` and it writes both files.
/backend/.env
/apps/insolvia_app/.env

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
# Where the retired Python brand-mark cutter kept its venv (the cutter is
# tool/cut-brand-marks.ts now). Still ignored so a checkout that ran it does
# not show the leftover; delete it freely. Anchored: one known path, not a
# licence for any `.cache` anywhere.
/.cache/

# ── Node (the npm workspace + the version-gated React packages) ─
# package-lock.json IS committed (reproducible npm installs in CI).
node_modules/
storybook-static/
# Build output is anchored per package rather than a bare `dist/`, which would
# silently swallow any future build directory anywhere in the repo. Each new
# Node package that builds adds its own line. (The design system deliberately
# has none: it publishes source — a package-side build would collapse its
# .web/.native leaf pairs.)
/apps/insolvia_admin/dist/

# Tool-run artifacts that may sit on disk while a branch that does not track
# their package is checked out (the per-app .gitignore only exists on branches
# where the app does). Ignoring them at the root keeps a `git add -A` from a
# different branch from sweeping them into an unrelated commit.
.lighthouseci/
.react-router/
# ── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/

# ── agent skills: installed, not vendored ───────────────────────
# `skills-lock.json` (tracked) is the manifest; `scripts/dev-setup.sh` installs
# from it with the `skills` CLI. The files themselves are third-party
# documentation we neither wrote nor review, so they stay out of the tree — see
# the `.agents/skills/` section in CLAUDE.md.
#
# `.claude/skills/` is NOT ignored wholesale: `insolvia-*` are OUR skills and
# stay tracked. Only the symlinks the installer drops there are ignored, by the
# names the lock installs.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/design-system-*
.claude/skills/expo-*
.claude/skills/eas-*
# The .NET skills for backend/ — dotnet/skills (Microsoft) and
# Aaronontheweb/dotnet-skills — have no common prefix either; one line each.
.claude/skills/analyzing-dotnet-performance
.claude/skills/api-design
.claude/skills/assertion-quality
.claude/skills/csharp-concurrency-patterns
.claude/skills/csharp-expert
.claude/skills/csharp-refactoring
.claude/skills/database-performance
